From: Muhammad Huda Nugroho <mhudan21@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] bus: mhi: pci_generic: enlarge IP_HW0 HW channel rings to 512

The generic modem_qcom_v1 config gives the hardware-accelerated IP_HW0 UL/DL
channels only 128 ring descriptors. On the Quectel RG520N-EB (SDX6x) over a
busy IPQ5018 this is too shallow: under sustained downlink the DL ring drains
below the refill threshold and empties before the host can refill it, and the
modem's hardware DL (IPA) engine then deadlocks on descriptor starvation and
stops forever until a modem reset (rx frozen, tx ok, link up).

Qualcomm's own vendor pcie_mhi driver uses 512 (NUM_MHI_IPA_IN/OUT_RING_ELEMENTS),
and mainline already uses 512 for other SDX6x modems (e.g. the Telit/Sierra
profiles in this file). Match that: 512 x 16-byte TRE = 8 KiB of ring, trivial
DMA memory, 4x more headroom for the host to keep the ring fed. The dedicated
HW DL event ring (2048) already satisfies the "event >= 2x channel" rule.

Signed-off-by: Muhammad Huda Nugroho <mhudan21@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/bus/mhi/host/pci_generic.c
+++ b/drivers/bus/mhi/host/pci_generic.c
@@ -318,8 +318,8 @@ static const struct mhi_channel_config modem_qcom_v1_mhi_channels[] = {
 	MHI_CHANNEL_CONFIG_UL(46, "IP_SW0", 64, 2),
 	MHI_CHANNEL_CONFIG_DL(47, "IP_SW0", 64, 3),
-	MHI_CHANNEL_CONFIG_HW_UL(100, "IP_HW0", 128, 4),
-	MHI_CHANNEL_CONFIG_HW_DL(101, "IP_HW0", 128, 5),
+	MHI_CHANNEL_CONFIG_HW_UL(100, "IP_HW0", 512, 4),
+	MHI_CHANNEL_CONFIG_HW_DL(101, "IP_HW0", 512, 5),
 };

 static struct mhi_event_config modem_qcom_v1_mhi_events[] = {
